// The gateway's model, as it is actually configured (2026-10-12). Applying it changes
// nothing on the current gateway; use it to restore the model after experiments.
// Run from openclaw-gateway-docker:
//   docker compose exec -T openclaw-gateway node dist/index.js config patch --stdin --dry-run < ../openclaw-express/openclaw-model-pin.json5
//   docker compose exec -T openclaw-gateway node dist/index.js config patch --stdin < ../openclaw-express/openclaw-model-pin.json5
//
// - Groq gpt-oss-120b is the only model. Llama 3.3 was retired from Groq.
// - No fallbacks: when Groq returns 429, the gateway retries the same model (up to 9 times,
//   ~50 s apart). Adding a fallback is an open decision (local Ollama, Cerebras, or a paid provider).
// - gpt-oss-120b is a reasoning model. `npm run whatsapp:sync` sets
//   agents.defaults.thinkingDefault = "low" to keep its hidden reasoning short, and
//   src/utils/sanitizeChatAnswer.js strips reasoning that leaks into Express answers.
// - Free tier: 8,000 tokens per minute and 200,000 per day for this model (per Groq
//   organization). One reply costs ~2,900 input tokens; see CLAUDE.md "Token budget".

{
  agents: {
    defaults: {
      model: {
        primary: "groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b",
        fallbacks: [],
      },
    },
  },
}
